      "score": 91,
      "summary": "B is the strongest overall. It ranks findings P1 and P2, states what is set aside, and labels every runtime unknown. On the technical side it derives origin from resolved placement including flips, reverses reopen from the current opacity, captures the displayed position on re-grab, and requires a trace before any performance claim. Each plan maps to the findings it covers and has a precise drift stop. One small drawback is the optional momentum projection gate, which is a mild scope addition."
