      "score": 90,
      "summary": "C shows the best restraint on purpose and frequency: it removes the palette animation entirely. It is careful about technical limits, noting that a centered origin and the custom-property write are not proven defects, and it gives concrete token-based CSS. Its queue plan, however, introduces a spring with a 0.4s response that is not tied to the existing tokens. That slightly weakens convention reuse and technical grounding."
